# Skill-local LF pin. Keep in sync with the repository-root .gitattributes.
#
# Why this file exists twice: this skill's gates hash worktree bytes, not git
# blobs. scripts/verify_case_hashes.py compares sha256 of the checked-out file
# against registry.json / case.json manifests, and the trigger eval ledger
# records evaluated_skill_md_sha256 for SKILL.md. On Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true a plain checkout materializes CRLF, which changes those
# hashes and fails the gates on line endings alone - indistinguishable from real
# tampering. Verified once already: a CRLF checkout of one case.json produced
# e87142de instead of the recorded 0894dcf6.
#
# The root file pins these paths for this repository. This copy makes the pin
# travel with the directory, so vendoring the skill into another repository or
# copying it into ~/.claude/skills/ cannot silently lose the guarantee. Blobs are
# already LF, so this changes no committed bytes - only what checkout writes.
#
# Suffix list must match EOL_CHECKED_SUFFIXES in scripts/validate_architecture.py.

.gitattributes text eol=lf

*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.cjs  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.tsv  text eol=lf

# Extensionless text file: not covered by the suffix rules above.
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending convert.
*.wasm binary
*.pt   binary
